  "title": "Integrating ST67W611M1A6U wifi chip to the Stm32 Nucleo-H753ZI board",
  "content": "<p>Hi. We are encountering issues whilst the integration of st67w611m1a6u wifi chip to the Stm Nucleo-H753zi board(host) using SPI for communication and UART for debug logs. The Wi-Fi module firmware has been successfully loaded, but the network driver does not initialize on the host. As a result, the module cannot connect to a Wi-Fi network. We would be pleased to receive more clarity on this. The zip file of our project has been attached below and necessary files are also added.<br /><br />Pin connections between st67 wifi chip and nucleo board</p><div class=\"widget-toc\"></div><p> </p><table><thead><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">wifi IC</th>\t\t\t<th style=\"width:189px;\">nucleo board </th>\t\t</tr></thead><tbody><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">VDDIO</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">3.3v</td>\t\t</tr><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">VDD33</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">3.3v</td>\t\t</tr><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">GND</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">GND</td>\t\t</tr><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">CHIP_EN</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">PE2</td>\t\t</tr><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">BOOT</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">PE4</td>\t\t</tr><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">SPI_RDY</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">PE3</td>\t\t</tr><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">SPI_CS</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">PA4</td>\t\t</tr><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">SPI_CLK</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">PA5</td>\t\t</tr><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">SPI_MISO</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">PA6</td>\t\t</tr><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">SPI_MOSI</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">PA7</td>\t\t</tr><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">UART_TX</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">PD8</td>\t\t</tr><tr><th style=\"width:160px;\">UART_RX</th>\t\t\t<td style=\"width:189px;\">PD9</td>\t\t</tr></tbody></table><div class=\"widget-toc toc_root\"></div>",
